            { q: 'Can you go up Golghar’s stairs?', a: 'This review could not confirm that the top is currently open. 2026 repair reports mention a long-standing restriction on the stairs and plans to reopen them. The historical description of 145 steps is not today’s permission; check the current situation on site.' },
            { q: 'Who built Golghar and when?', a: 'According to the Patna district administration’s history account, Captain John Garstin had the granary built for the British army in 1786. It was connected to a grain-storage plan after the 1770 famine.' },
            { q: 'How many steps does Golghar have?', a: 'The Patna district administration mentions 145 winding steps. That is a historical description of the architecture, not today’s permission to climb. Check the entrance and the condition of the stairs through local instructions.' },
            { q: 'How tall is Golghar?', a: 'The district administration’s account gives a height of about 29 metres and walls about 3.6 metres thick at the base. The building is described as a granary without pillars.' },
